WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:08.410
What is motorbike insurance? Motorbike insurance
is a legal requirement for any motorcyclist

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:11.549
riding on the roads in the UK; it helps to
cover the costs should you be involved in

00:00:11.549 --> 00:00:19.090
a road accident. Just as with any motor insurance
policy, there are different levels of cover

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:24.070
to choose from, from third party up to fully
comprehensive. You should always compare different

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:28.689
policies very carefully to make sure you get
right the level of cover you need. When looking

00:00:28.689 --> 00:00:33.120
at different policies, you’ll need to consider
the type of motorcycle you have, how often

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:38.410
you use it and what you can afford to pay
in annual premiums and other potential costs.

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:42.170
Different providers will also offer benefits
and extras, helping you to tailor your policy

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:47.480
to suit your needs and your motorbike.

